Courier (apps/desktop/courier): compile github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3's bundled
SQLite with FTS5, for the engine's search index.

Upstream turns FTS5 on only under the sqlite_fts5 build tag
(sqlite3_opt_fts5.go), which gazelle leaves out of the generated go_library.
This adds that file's two cgo flags to the go_library instead, so FTS5 is a
property of the dependency rather than of a build flag:

- BUILD.bazel (generated by gazelle; go_repository applies patches after
  gazelle runs): -DSQLITE_ENABLE_FTS5 in copts and -lm in clinkopts (FTS5's
  bm25 ranking calls log()).

--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
         "static_mock.go",
     ],
     cgo = True,
-    clinkopts = select({
+    clinkopts = ["-lm"] + select({
         "@io_bazel_rules_go//go/platform:android": [
             "-ldl",
         ],
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@
         "-DSQLITE_DEFAULT_WAL_SYNCHRONOUS=1",
         "-DSQLITE_ENABLE_FTS3",
         "-DSQLITE_ENABLE_FTS3_PARENTHESIS",
+        "-DSQLITE_ENABLE_FTS5",
         "-DSQLITE_ENABLE_RTREE",
         "-DSQLITE_ENABLE_UPDATE_DELETE_LIMIT",
         "-DSQLITE_OMIT_DEPRECATED",
